Track 2: Sledge Hammered (Wait, Is The Ice Still Singing?)
- Story & Context: Kael sits alone in the comms-tower, recording the sound of the metal rafters warping under the pressure of a localized freak blizzard. She presses her ear against the steel, hearing the moans of the architecture and the rhythmic clicking of the automated heat-regulators struggling to survive. She doesn't know who she’s confessing to, but she records a melody of isolation and asks, "How long before the silence becomes the song?" as her fingers trace the jagged line where the ice has cracked the floorboard.
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: A close-up of a human eye reflecting a chaotic, swirling blizzard outside a thick, scratched polycarbonate window, captured in moody, desaturated greys and deep winter blues.

Track 3: The Perma-Frostbite Protocol
- Story & Context: Generations after the Great Stasis, the children of the North recount the tale of the Architect who walked into the tundra and simply stopped. Legend says his heart still beats at 40 BPM beneath the glacier, providing the low-frequency tremor that allows the arctic moss to bloom in the dark. It is the myth of the ending, where "we finally learned how to stop the shaking," an aftermath where humanity ceased striving and began simply existing in the rhythmic peace of the deep freeze.
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: A monumental, ghostly silhouette of a human figure half-submerged in a massive, translucent wall of blue ice, glowing with internal, dying circuits.

